      "comment": "FLYING JACKIE (1) boasts the best exposed form, placing in both starts, including a third at Kilmore over 2180m, where she was beaten three and a half metres by Catch A Butterfly. She also bested JASPER JAY there, which is relevant for this field, and gate one enhances her chances. LOCHINVAR CHANDON (3) drops in class, returning after the Listed Woodlands Stud Nutrien Classic Sales Race Series 5 2Yo Pacing Fillies Final at Riverina Paceway, where Kahula clocked a sharp 1:53.0. Her recent win at Shepparton in a trial sets her up nicely for this maiden. BLAKE TREVOR (9) showed promise on debut, finishing second to Del Licious at Riverina Paceway and beating MACHETE RANGER. He looks like an improving contender. BREAKING NEWS (2) returns from Listed races after three trials, with her last being a second at Coolamon, but she faced heavy defeats in her two races, so the class drop should help.",
